WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:04.640
In the previous videos,

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:08.680
we learnt that it is possible to have square root of a negative number,

00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:11.340
but it involved using a new number 'i',

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:14.820
which is equal to the square root of negative 1.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:17.980
These numbers are called imaginary numbers

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:21.700
and could be of the form 'bi' where 'b' is a real number.

00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:25.480
And 'i' is equal square root of negative 1.

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:31.840
Numbers like 'i', '2i', 'negative 4i' are all imaginary numbers!

00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:35.580
What if we have a number like 3 plus 7i ?

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:38.400
Will this be an imaginary number?

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:42.300
Well, we can be sure that this part of the number is imaginary.

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:44.920
And this part is a real number.

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:48.740
So this is a mix of real and imaginary parts.

00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:52.260
And this is what we call an example of a complex number.

00:00:52.580 --> 00:00:56.560
Real plus imaginary gives us a complex number.

00:00:56.560 --> 00:00:59.640
It's of the form 'a' plus 'bi'

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:02.040
where 'a' and 'b' are real numbers,

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:04.840
and 'i' is the unit imaginary number.

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:08.120
Now let's play around with this basic form.

00:01:08.380 --> 00:01:11.060
Observe that when 'a' is equal to '0',

00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:14.080
what is left will be an imaginary number.

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:18.580
And when 'b' is equal to '0' we only have a real number.

00:01:18.940 --> 00:01:21.400
So what are the real and imaginary parts,

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:24.160
in the basic form of a complex number?

00:01:24.380 --> 00:01:29.980
'a' is called the real part and 'bi' is called the imaginary part.

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:32.680
Now let me ask you something interesting!

00:01:33.140 --> 00:01:35.300
When will the two complex numbers

00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:38.580
'a' plus 'bi' and 'c' plus 'di' be equal?

00:01:45.160 --> 00:01:49.500
They will be equal only if both the conditions are satisfied.

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:51.760
First 'a' is equal to 'c'

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:54.760
and second 'b' is equal to 'd'.

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:58.800
Yes, only if 'a is equal to c' and 'b is equal to d'

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:01.780
will the two complex numbers be equal.

00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:06.840
Real parts equal and the imaginary parts as well are equal.

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:10.140
However, the real numbers are comprehensible.

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:13.300
Why are we moving towards complex numbers?

00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:16.020
Do they lead to anything worthwhile?

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:17.700
There were doubts about it.

00:02:17.720 --> 00:02:21.640
Even among mathematicians who initially developed this concept.

00:02:21.860 --> 00:02:24.140
While some did not believe in them.

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:27.860
Others were desperately trying to prove their existence.

00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:29.860
Still the journey continued

00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:34.120
and complex numbers were finally allowed by mathematicians.

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:39.020
Today, the most people may find complex numbers incomprehensible

00:02:39.020 --> 00:02:40.680
or difficult to understand.

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:42.860
They do exist in some form

00:02:42.860 --> 00:02:46.060
and serve the purpose of understanding of nature.

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:49.520
Engineers use it to study stresses on beams,

00:02:49.540 --> 00:02:51.140
phenomena of resonance

00:02:51.140 --> 00:02:55.560
and the flow of fluid around objects, such as water around a pipe.

00:02:55.840 --> 00:02:57.520
They make it easy to understand

00:02:57.520 --> 00:03:00.420
the flow of current through electronic circuits,

00:03:00.420 --> 00:03:04.420
using resistances, inductance and capacitors.

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:07.540
They are also used in electromagnetism,

00:03:07.540 --> 00:03:09.420
where rather than trying to describe an

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:13.300
electromagnetic field by two real quantities separately.

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:16.320
They are described as a single complex number,

00:03:16.360 --> 00:03:18.560
of which electric and magnetic

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:22.620
components are simply the real and imaginary parts.

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:24.960
How exactly are they used here?

00:03:24.980 --> 00:03:27.340
Well, it's an advanced topic

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:30.940
which we will cover in a graduation level math videos.

